{"chunk_id": "4c0b9efe1537", "text": "In exile, the Pandavas relocate from Dwaitavana to the forest of Kamyaka after Vyasa advises Yudhishthira. Before leaving, Vyasa imparts a powerful body of knowledge to Yudhishthira, which he preserves and recites. Living austerely in Kamyaka with many Brahmanas, the brothers hunt, practice archery, and perform sacred rites. Remembering Vyasa\u2019s counsel, Yudhishthira privately summons Arjuna and explains the strategic danger they face: the greatest masters of arms\u2014Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, Karna, and Ashwatthama\u2014stand with Duryodhana. Since Arjuna is their chief hope, Yudhishthira instructs him to undertake severe asceticism and seek Indra to obtain celestial weapons. Armed with the Gandiva and blessed by Brahmanas and Draupadi, Arjuna departs northward to gain divine power for the coming war, marking the beginning of his quest for heavenly arms.\nYudhishthira instructs Arjuna to perform austerities and seek Indra to obtain celestial weapons for the future war against Duryodhana.\nThemes: quest for divine weapons, brotherly duty, preparation for war, ascetic austerity, farewell and blessings", "vector": [-0.0004933885647915304, -0.024981698021292686, -0.0044234259985387325, 0.01227101031690836, -0.0028329244814813137, 0.038931477814912796, -0.020864713937044144, -0.004340153653174639, -0.015588579699397087, -0.022037189453840256, 0.009439751505851746, 0.00134817895013839, 0.015748461708426476, 0.010359077714383602, -0.005872364621609449, 0.0033475474920123816, 0.03701288253068924, -0.014536017552018166, 0.026500586420297623, -0.02412899024784565, -0.01193125918507576, -0.010678843595087528, 0.009852781891822815, 0.025674523785710335, -0.006718411576002836, 0.00864033680409193, 0.00876691099256277, -0.015042313374578953, -0.0021750731393694878, -0.012404246255755424, -0.011171815916895866, 0.008080746978521347, 0.00797415804117918, -0.0010109260911121964, -0.034508053213357925, 0.0011141836876049638, -0.014975695870816